phase.","style":"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["gradual_refinement","incremental_adjustments","feedback_driven","reflection_in_action","iterative_reflection_cycles"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Claude","purpose":"Design critique and feedback","interaction_type":"Analytical dialogue","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"GitHub Copilot","purpose":"Design system coding","interaction_type":"Component generation","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Concretizing vague requirements and finding specific examples","effectiveness":0.7470360031576024,"reasoning":"Leveraging AI to clarify fuzzy requirements and generate concrete examples from vague descriptions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":56.5489703150611,"cognitive_load":5.151942556962105,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":5,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":30.6,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection","cognitive_style":"reflective","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Style frames approved, palette's locked — now animate. Choreograph scene to scene. This transition, 'flow between services' — does that mean the icons morph into each other, or a clean cut with a wipe? Two totally different feels. Morph says 'connected system'; cut says 'clear steps.' For a general audience... I'll go morph on the related pair, hard cut between episodes. Rig the reusable icon components so I'm not rebuilding. Scene one moving. Reads smooth.","enhanced_requirements":["Finalize prototypes for Motion Graphics","Ensure quality standards are met for Motion Graphics","Prepare handoff documentation for Motion Graphics"],"original_requirements":["Finalize prototypes","Ensure quality standards are met","Prepare handoff documentation"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Key terms in Voiceover Integration lack precise definitions or measurable criteria","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Transforming fuzzy requirement