ine's animated logo.","artifact":"Review feedback","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on tacit in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering tight timeline"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":57,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Tacit","Resolved through Applied to Sound Design in Motion Graphics context"],"iteration_count":3,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved with minor revisions"}},{"phase_number":6,"phase_name":"Motion Testing","complexity":"Medium","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","requirements":["Preview animation on target platforms","Check playback smoothness and loops","Fix timing and rendering glitches"],"duration_estimate":21,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 3: Storyboarding.","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","utterance":"Audio signature's on, whoosh sits under — now motion testing across platforms. Preview, check loops. One thing I need to know: does the loop version need a seamless cycle, or a hold-then-restart? On Instagram it'll auto-loop, so a hard cut back to build would jar. Let me test — yeah, the seam pops. Add a two-frame crossfade at the loop point. Playback smooth on web and mobile now. Fixed a timing hitch at frame 20. Clean.","continuity":" Transitioning from Vagueness in previous phase.","style":"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["leverage_past_cases","pragmatic_approach","iterative_testing","iterative_reflection_cycles","conversation_with_materials"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":52.40821464846668,"cognitive_load":7.788296251680208,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":5,"efficiency":4},"actual_duration":29.4,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection","cognitive_style":"reflective","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Audio signature's on, whoosh sits under — now motion testing across platforms. Preview, check loops. One thing I need to know: does the loop version need a seamless cycle, or a hold-then-restart? On Instagram it'll auto-loop, so a hard cut back to build would jar. Let me test — yeah, the seam pops. Add a two-frame crossfade at the loop point. Playback smooth on web and mobile now. Fixed a timing hitch at frame 20. Clean.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop motion testing based on previous phase for Motion Graphics","Consider budget constraints for Motion Graphics","Iterate based on feedback for Motion Graphics"],"original_requirements":["Develop motion testing based on previous phase","Consider budget constraints","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Multiple valid interpretations exist in Storyboarding due to competing stakeholder interests","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Managing multiple valid interpretations while maintaining design coherence","design_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection using reflective thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 21h allocated","Complexity: Medium","Dependencies: Design system"],"success_criteria":["Stakeholder approval achieved","Innovative solution delivered","User testing validation"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":3,"total_phases":8,"domain":"Motion Graphics","project_name":"Brand Animation Package","designer":"Designer_41","timestamp":"2024-01-06"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Approved","completion_date":"2024-10-05","sign_off":"Client approved"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Tested the animated logo playback across platforms and fixed loop and timing issues for Emberline.","artifact":"Design iterations","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on uncertainty in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":43,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Uncertainty","Resolved through Applied to Motion Testing in Motion Graphics context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved with minor revisions"}},{"phase_number":7,"phase_name":"Final Export","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Export logo animation formats","Package looping and static variants","Organize labeled delivery files"],"duration_estimate":40,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 5: Production.","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","utterance":"Playback's smooth, loop seams gone — now final export and package. 'Multiple formats' — which exactly? ProRes plus H.264 covers most, but do they need WebM for the site, GIF for email? Could read either way. I'll cover the likely set: ProRes master, H.264, transparent MOV, plus a GIF for lightweight use. Package looping and static variants, static PNG end-frame too. Labeled folders, dated. Packaged. Note listing formats included so they can ask if something's missing.","continuity":" Transitioning from Vagueness in previous phase.","style":"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["safe_choices","proven_patterns","incremental_optimization","conversation_with_materials"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Claude","purpose":"Research synthesis","interaction_type":"Information processing","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Figma AI","purpose":"Prototype interactions","interaction_type":"Smart animate","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.8778264284086519,"reasoni