achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Approved","completion_date":"2024-02-07","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Developed concept sketches for a daylit unit mix and energy-efficient massing suited to urban professionals.","artifact":"Research documents","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on uncertainty in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering budget constraints"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":43,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Uncertainty","Resolved through Applied to Concept Development in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":3,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":3,"phase_name":"Schematic Design","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Tacit","requirements":["Lay out typical floor plans and unit types","Design elevations and building massing","Locate cores and vertical circulation"],"duration_estimate":40,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 4: Schematic Design.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Concept's approved, flexible core reads well even with the ratio still open. Schematic now. Laying out the typical floor — double-loaded corridor just feels right for this width, can't fully argue it over a point-block but the plate wants it. Units to the light, corridor tucked to the shaded north edge. Elevations follow the unit rhythm. Core and stair to code, one exit each end. Massing model built. Something about the proportion of that top setback isn't sitting right yet — I'll nudge it. Schematic set's produced.","continuity":" Transitioning from Ambiguity in previous phase.","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["externalize_knowledge","systematic_documentation","pattern_extraction","reflection_in_action"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":54.5763862591721,"cognitive_load":7.336505108968066,"satisfaction":5,"quality":5,"innovation":3,"efficiency":4},"actual_duration":36,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection","cognitive_style":"reflective","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Concept's approved, flexible core reads well even with the ratio still open. Schematic now. Laying out the typical floor — double-loaded corridor just feels right for this width, can't fully argue it over a point-block but the plate wants it. Units to the light, corridor tucked to the shaded north edge. Elevations follow the unit rhythm. Core and stair to code, one exit each end. Massing model built. Something about the proportion of that top setback isn't sitting right yet — I'll nudge it. Schematic set's produced.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop schematic design based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider tight timeline for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Develop schematic design based on previous phase","Consider tight timeline","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Success in Schematic Design relies heavily on experiential knowledge and intuition","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Articulating intuitive design decisions for stakeholder buy-in","design_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection using reflective thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 40h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Stakeholder approval"],"success_criteria":["High quality standards met","Technical feasibility confirmed","Stakeholder approval achieved"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":4,"total_phases":8,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Residential Building Design","designer":"Designer_44","timestamp":"2024-12-15"},"deliverables":["Floor plans","Elevations","Sections","Massing model"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Some creative elements incorporated","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Approved","completion_date":"2024-10-09","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Produced schematic floor plans, elevations, and a massing model organizing the multi-family unit types.","artifact":"Floor plans","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on tacit in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Floor plans","Elevations","Sections","Massing model"],"progress_percentage":57,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Tacit","Resolved through Applied to Schematic Design in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved"}},{"phase_number":4,"phase_name":"Design Development","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","requirements":["Refine wall assemblies for energy efficiency","Detail unit interiors and party walls","Coordinate MEP with structural sections"],"duration_estimate":39,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 6: Construction Documents.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Schematic's locked, that top setback finally sits right. Design development now, the envelope. \"Energy efficient\" wall — to what standard? Code minimum, or push toward passive-house numbers? That's a real range and it changes the assembly depth. I'll target well above code, continuous exterior insulation, mineral wool, without going full passive on the budget. Detail the party walls for acoustics between units. Coordinate MEP risers with the structural section so nothing clashes. Wall sections drawn. Envelope's developing.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influen