penetrations, lock the schedules.","continuity":" Transitioning from Tacit in previous phase.","style":"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["safe_choices","proven_patterns","incremental_optimization","paradigm_shift_thinking","frame_creation"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Claude","purpose":"Design critique and feedback","interaction_type":"Analytical dialogue","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Design iteration","interaction_type":"ControlNet guidance","satisfaction":5}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.6649512018455433,"reasoning":"Utilizing AI to gather missing information and explore potential scenarios under uncertainty"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":73.07476870350014,"cognitive_load":10.597642240191258,"satisfaction":5,"quality":3,"innovation":3,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":34.5,"phase_insights":["High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Creates entirely new frames for understanding problems","cognitive_style":"transformative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Renders are approved, block reads well. Now CDs — and the real question is how much separation between retail and the apartments above. One-hour rating, or push to two? Code minimum, or a notch safer for the acoustic hit too. It's a dial — more mass, quieter units, but I eat floor-to-floor height. I'll take the two-hour assembly at the transfer level, one-hour elsewhere, and detail the resilient channel below the units. Coordinate the MEP penetrations, lock the schedules.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop technical drawings based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider budget constraints for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Develop technical drawings based on previous phase","Consider budget constraints","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Critical information needed for Technical Coordination is not yet available","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Making progress despite missing critical information","design_approach":"Creates entirely new frames for understanding problems using transformative thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 39h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: User research"],"success_criteria":["Design principles maintained","User testing validation","Technical feasibility confirmed"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":6,"total_phases":6,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Mixed-Use Urban Development","designer":"Designer_45","timestamp":"2024-03-22"},"deliverables":["Construction documents","Detail drawings","Specifications","Schedules"],"outcome_summary":["Acceptable quality standards met","Some creative elements incorporated","Timeline challenges encountered","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"In Review","completion_date":"2024-03-19","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Produced coordinated construction documents detailing the fire and acoustic separations between mixed uses.","artifact":"Construction documents","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on vagueness in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering tight timeline"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Construction documents","Detail drawings","Specifications","Schedules"],"progress_percentage":75,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Vagueness","Resolved through Applied to Technical Drawings in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved with minor revisions"}},{"phase_number":8,"phase_name":"Documentation","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","requirements":["Assemble permit submission drawing set","Compile specifications and schedules","Package final client deliverables"],"duration_estimate":37,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 7: Documentation","cogniti