 Commons Residential-Over-Retail","domain":"Architecture","phases":[{"phase_number":1,"phase_name":"Concept Development","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Explore commercial-over-residential massing ideas","Study flexible ground-floor layouts","Sketch neighborhood-scaled concept options"],"duration_estimate":44,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 5: Detailed Design.","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","utterance":"Fresh brief — Marlowe Neighborhood Builders, mid-scale, housing over flexible commercial ground space, growing neighborhood. \"Flexible\" is the word I keep turning. Flexible how — one big shell a tenant subdivides later, or pre-zoned bays with cores already dropped? Café versus clinic versus retail want very different things. Fifteen years tells me don't over-commit the ground floor. I'll sketch massing with housing set back over a tall, mostly-open commercial base, and study a couple of ground layouts — open shell and lightly-serviced bays. Neighborhood-scaled, not looming.","continuity":" Transitioning from Tacit in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["create_multiple_variations","visual_experimentation","broad_exploration","bounded_rationality_acceptance"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Design iteration","interaction_type":"ControlNet guidance","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"GitHub Copilot","purpose":"Documentation generation","interaction_type":"Comment completion","satisfaction":3}],"purpose":"Concretizing vague requirements and finding specific examples","effectiveness":0.9312900604597667,"reasoning":"Leveraging AI to clarify fuzzy requirements and generate concrete examples from vague descriptions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":54.54506725188087,"cognitive_load":8.321000619803474,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":4,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":44.9,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Fresh brief — Marlowe Neighborhood Builders, mid-scale, housing over flexible commercial ground space, growing neighborhood. \"Flexible\" is the word I keep turning. Flexible how — one big shell a tenant subdivides later, or pre-zoned bays with cores already dropped? Café versus clinic versus retail want very different things. Fifteen years tells me don't over-commit the ground floor. I'll sketch massing with housing set back over a tall, mostly-open commercial base, and study a couple of ground layouts — open shell and lightly-serviced bays. Neighborhood-scaled, not looming.","enhanced_requirements":["Finalize prototypes for Architecture","Ensure quality standards are met for Architecture","Prepare handoff documentation for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Finalize prototypes","Ensure quality standards are met","Prepare handoff documentation"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"The boundaries and success metrics for Detailed Design are fuzzy and subjective","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Transforming fuzzy requirements into concrete design decisions","design_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions using analytical_pragmatic thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 44h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Stakeholder approval"],"success_criteria":["Technical feasibility confirmed","User testing validation","Design principles maintained"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":5,"total_phases":6,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Mixed-Use Urban Development","designer":"Designer_46","timestamp":"2024-04-24"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Delivered within timeline","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"In Review","completion_date":"2024-03-05","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Developed concepts placing residential units above flexible commercial ground space for the growing neighborhood.","artifact":"Final deliverables","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering tight timeline"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":100,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Concept Development in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":2,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":2,"phase_name":"Schematic Design","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","requirements":["Lay out flexible ground-floor commercial plan","Model mid-scale building massing","Draft elevations and sections"],"duration_estimate":37,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 3: Master Planning.","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","utterance":"Concepts down — housing over an open base. Now schematic plans. What I don't have yet is the anchor tenant's actual demising needs, so I can't fix where the party walls and second exit land on the ground floor. I'll plan it as a clear-span shell with the exits and utility spine positioned so tenants can carve it either way, and note the demising as future. Model the mid-scale massing, draft elevations and sections. Design the flexibility in rather than guess the tenant.","continuity":" Transitioning from Vagueness in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["prepare_multiple_scenarios","hypothesis_testing","parallel_prototyping","bounded_rationality_acceptance"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"GitHub Copilot","purpose":"Design system coding","interaction_type":"Component generation","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"Midjourney","purpose":"Aesthetic exploration","interaction_type":"Style prompting","satisfaction":5}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.8767757965850633,"reasoning":"Utilizing AI to gather missing information and explore potential scenarios under uncertainty"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":49.24952473662066,"cognitive_load":10.25908440719129,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":3,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":40.9,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Concepts down — housing over an open base. Now schematic plans. What I don't have yet is the anchor tenant's actual demising needs, so I can't fix where the party walls and second exit land on the ground floor. I'll plan it as a clear-span shell with the exits and utility spine positioned so tenants can carve it either way, and note the demising as future. Model the mid-scale massing, draft elevations and sections. Design the flexibility in rather than guess the tenant.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop schematic design based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider budget constraints for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Develop schematic design based on previous phase","Consider budget constraints","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"External dependencies and unknowns block decision-making in Master Planning","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Making progress despite missing critical information","design_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions using analytical_pragmatic thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 37h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Technical specs"],"success_criteria":["High quality standards met","Technical feasibility confirmed","User testing validation"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":3,"total_phases":6,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Mixed-Use Urban Development","designer":"Designer_46","timestamp":"2024-02-10"},"deliverables":["Floor plans","Elevations","Sections","Massing model"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Some creative elements incorporated","Delivered within timeline","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"In Review","completion_date":"2024-04-08","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Produced schematic plans and massing integrating residential floors above adaptable commercial ground space.","artifact":"Sections","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on uncertainty in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering tight timeline"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Floor plans","Elevations","Sections","Massing model"],"progress_percentage":60,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Uncertainty","Resolved through Applied to Schematic Design in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":2,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved"}},{"phase_number":3,"phase_name":"Design Development","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Detail flexible commercial tenant partitions","Resolve residential unit wall sections","Refine coordinated 3D model"],"duration_estimate":44,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 1: Urban Context Study.","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","utterance":"Massing and schematics hold. Now detailed plans and wall sections. The commercial partitions — \"flexible\" again. Demountable so a tenant reconfigures in a weekend, or just non-loadbearing studs that move with a real renovation? Different cost, different promise. I'll draw the tenant partitions as non-loadbearing on a raised track, easy to relocate but not gimmicky. Resolve the residential wall sections above — proper thermal and acoustic layup — and refine the coordinated 3D model so the base and the units actually line up.","continuity":"","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["explore_multiple_interpretations","create_divergent_options","delay_decisions","bounded_rationality_acceptance","problem_decomposition"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Midjourney","purpose":"Material and texture studies","interaction_type":"Detail refinement","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Style transfer","interaction_type":"Image-to-image","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Exploring multiple interpretations and generating diverse options","effectiveness":0.865408233506068,"reasoning":"Using AI to explore multiple interpretations and generate diverse solutions for ambiguous requirements"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":49.31792478783746,"cognitive_load":9.49719439195805,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":5,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":52.4,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Massing and schematics hold. Now detailed plans and wall sections. The commercial partitions — \"flexible\" again. Demountable so a tenant reconfigures in a weekend, or just non-loadbearing studs that move with a real renovation? Different cost, different promise. I'll draw the tenant partitions as non-loadbearing on a raised track, easy to relocate but not gimmicky. Resolve the residential wall sections above — proper thermal and acoustic layup — and refine the coordinated 3D model so the base and the units actually line up.","enhanced_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution for Architecture","Address unclear requirements for Architecture","Define project scope and constraints for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution","Address unclear requirements","Define project scope and constraints"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Conflicting constraints in Architecture create genuine ambiguity about the right approach","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Managing multiple valid interpretations while maintaining design coherence","design_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions using analytical_pragmatic thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 44h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Technical specs"],"success_criteria":["Innovative solution delivered","High quality standards met","User testing validation"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":1,"total_phases":6,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Mixed-Use Urban Development","designer":"Designer_46","timestamp":"2024-08-11"},"deliverables":["Detailed plans","Building sections","Wall sections","3D model"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Delivered within timeline","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Completed","completion_date":"2024-09-02","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Developed detailed plans and wall sections for the flexible commercial base and residential units above.","artifact":"3D model","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Detailed plans","Building sections","Wall sections","3D model"],"progress_percentage":20,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Design Development in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved with minor revisions"}},{"phase_number":4,"phase_name":"Material Specification","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Tacit","requirements":["Specify durable ground-floor commercial finishes","Match residential facade material palette","Confirm acoustic separation between uses"],"duration_estimate":43,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 4: Sustainability Analysis.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Sections resolved, model's coordinated. Materials now. Brick on the residential mass — I know it's right the moment I put it against the storefront glazing below. Can't fully justify it over metal panel on cost; it just carries the family, permanent, settled feeling this neighborhood reads as home. The glass base stays light and commercial, the brick above stays grounded. Then the floor between — I'll specify a proper acoustic assembly so nobody hears the shop below. Match the palette, confirm the separation.","continuity":" Transitioning from Uncertainty in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["intuitive_exploration","creative_experimentation","trust_instinct","problem_decomposition","satisficing_approach"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":56.96659749021981,"cognitive_load":6.9667246014176225,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":3,"efficiency":5},"actual_duration":38.7,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","Quality improvement from previous phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Sections resolved, model's coordinated. Materials now. Brick on the residential mass — I know it's right the moment I put it against the storefront glazing below. Can't fully justify it over metal panel on cost; it just carries the family, permanent, settled feeling this neighborhood reads as home. The glass base stays light and commercial, the brick above stays grounded. Then the floor between — I'll specify a proper acoustic assembly so nobody hears the shop below. Match the palette, confirm the separation.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop material specification based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider budget constraints for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Develop material specification based on previous phase","Consider budget constraints","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Success in Sustainability Analysis relies heavily on experiential knowledge and intuition","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Articulating intuitive design decisions for stakeholder buy-in","design_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions using analytical_pragmatic thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 43h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: User research"],"success_criteria":["Technical feasibility confirmed","High quality standards met","Stakeholder approval achieved"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":4,"total_phases":6,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Mixed-Use Urban Development","designer":"Designer_46","timestamp":"2024-09-17"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Some creative elements incorporated","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"In Review","completion_date":"2024-09-28","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Specified brick facade, storefront glazing, and acoustic floor assemblies separating shops from apartments above.","artifact":"Review feedback","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on tacit in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering budget constraints"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":80,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Tacit","Resolved through Applied to Material Specification in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved"}},{"phase_number":5,"phase_name":"Documentation","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","requirements":["Compile permit set for mixed-use building","Coordinate commercial and residential code sheets","Issue final drawings to Marlowe Neighborhood Builders"],"duration_estimate":46,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 2: Stakeholder Engagement.","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","utterance":"Brick and glazing set, acoustic floor confirmed. Final permit set now. Question is how much of the mixed-occupancy code analysis goes on the sheets versus how much the reviewer takes as read. Belt-and-suspenders, or trust the code-plan summary? For a mixed-use in front of a plans examiner I lean thorough — dedicate the code sheets, spell out occupancy separation and egress per use. Coordinate the commercial and residential sheets so they don't fight, then compile and issue to Marlowe Neighborhood Builders. Done.","continuity":" Transitioning from Ambiguity in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["create_multiple_variations","visual_experimentation","broad_exploration","bounded_rationality_acceptance","problem_decomposition"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"GitHub Copilot","purpose":"Code implementation","interaction_type":"Code completion","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Style transfer","interaction_type":"Image-to-image","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Concretizing vague requirements and finding specific examples","effectiveness":0.8141041601046591,"reasoning":"Leveraging AI to clarify fuzzy requirements and generate concrete examples from vague descriptions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":46.51277754857717,"cognitive_load":8.573624341559412,"satisfaction":5,"quality":3,"innovation":5,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":46.9,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Brick and glazing set, acoustic floor confirmed. Final permit set now. Question is how much of the mixed-occupancy code analysis goes on the sheets versus how much the reviewer takes as read. Belt-and-suspenders, or trust the code-plan summary? For a mixed-use in front of a plans examiner I lean thorough — dedicate the code sheets, spell out occupancy separation and egress per use. Coordinate the commercial and residential sheets so they don't fight, then compile and issue to Marlowe Neighborhood Builders. Done.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop documentation based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider budget constraints for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Develop documentation based on previous phase","Consider budget constraints","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Key terms in Stakeholder Engagement lack precise definitions or measurable criteria","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Transforming fuzzy requirements into concrete design decisions","design_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions using analytical_pragmatic thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 46h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Technical specs"],"success_criteria":["Stakeholder approval achieved","Innovative solution delivered","Design principles maintained"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":2,"total_phases":6,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Mixed-Use Urban Development","designer":"Designer_46","timestamp":"2024-05-19"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["Acceptable quality standards met","Innovative solutions developed","Delivered within timeline","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Completed","completion_date":"2024-04-24","sign_off":"Client approved"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Compiled the permit-ready construction set coordinating retail shell and residential unit drawings for Marlowe Neighborhood Builders.","artifact":"Final deliverables","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on vagueness in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering budget constraints"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":40,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Vagueness","Resolved through Applied to Documentation in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":2,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved"}}],"project_outcomes":{"avg_quality":53.85964539380862,"final_quality":66.56598054771577,"quality_trend":"improving","avg_cognitive_load":8.317514688327808,"total_duration":252.1,"state_transitions":["Ambiguity → Vagueness","Vagueness → Uncertainty","Uncertainty → Tacit","Tacit → Vagueness","Vagueness → Tacit"]},"persona_details":{"design_philosophy":"Parametric design with computational methods","primary_framework":"Cross","working_style":"Agile sprints with rapid prototyping","years_experience":15,"expertise_level":"Junior","ai_familiarity":"Intermediate","ai_usage_frequency":"Weekly"},"project_brief":{"client":"Marlowe Neighborhood Builders","client_type":"Government Agency","project_goal":"Design a mid-scale mixed-use building for Marlowe Neighborhood Builders that integrates residential units above flexible commercial ground space for a growing neighborhood.","target_users":"Primary demographic with specific needs in this domain","budget":"$273k","timeline":"7 months","key_requirements":["Flexible ground-floor commercial units","Residential floors above podium","Specify durable exterior cladding","Separate residential and retail access","Accessible common circulation","Coordinated design development set"],"constraints":["Budget limitations","Technical feasibility","Regulatory compliance","Timeline restrictions"],"success_metrics":["User satisfaction > 85%","Meet all functional requirements","On-time, on-budget delivery"]},"designer_profile":{"name":"Designer_46","experience_years":15,"expertise_level":"Junior","primary_framework":"Cross","design_philosophy":"Parametric design with computational methods","working_style":"Agile sprints with rapid prototyping","ai_usage":"Weekly","personality_type":"The Perfectionist","traits":["Detail-oriented","Methodical","Quality-focused","Sometimes overthinks"],"work_style":"Iterates multiple times until every detail is perfect. Often works late to refine designs.","strengths":["Exceptional attention to detail","High quality output","Thorough documentation"],"challenges":["Can miss deadlines due to perfectionism","Difficulty with 'good enough'"],"quote":"Design is in the details, and details make the difference.","tools_proficiency":["Figma","Sketch","Adobe Creative Suite","Prototyping tools","3D software"],"specializations":["User Research","Service Design"],"awards":[],"personality_description":"A meticulous designer who obsesses over every pixel and detail","design_approach":"Iterates countless times until achieving flawless execution. Often works late refining designs that others would consider complete.","key_strength":"Produces exceptionally polished work with zero compromises","key_weakness":"Can miss deadlines due to over-refinement","design_mindset":"Believes that good design is invisible and perfect design is memorable"},"final_outcome":{"final_deliverables":["Complete architecture package","Documentation and specifications","Final prototypes/mockups","Implementation guidelines","Project handoff materials"],"key_achievements":["Completed all 5 project phases on schedule","Met all key requirements identified in brief","Achieved target user satisfaction metrics","Delivered innovative architecture solution"],"challenges_overcome":["Resolved conflicting stakeholder requirements","Adapted to changing project constraints","Balanced innovation with practical limitations"],"client_feedback":"Professional execution with creative solutions that exceeded our expectations.","market_impact":"Setting new standards in architecture","next_steps":"Implementation and market launch planned"}},{"project_id":"project_47_7997","persona_id":47,"persona_name":"Designer_47","project_name":"Sunbrook Family Residences with Communal Courtyards","domain":"Architecture","phases":[{"phase_number":1,"phase_name":"Concept Development","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Sketch light-filled family unit concepts","Study shared courtyard and rooftop options","Test daylight orientation strategies"],"duration_estimate":47,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 1: Site Analysis.","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","utterance":"New project — Sunbrook Living, family building, spacious light-filled units, strong shared outdoor space. First concepts. \"Communal outdoor\" though — central courtyard the units wrap and overlook, or a rooftop the families ascend to? Courtyard gives eyes-on-kids, ground-level, everyday. Roof gives sun and view but it's a trip up. For families I lean courtyard as the heart. I'll sketch unit schemes with big windows, test a courtyard-wrapped scheme against a roof-terrace one, and check daylight orientation on each. Two directions to weigh.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["request_clarification","bracket_interpretations","systematic_analysis","satisficing_approach","bounded_rationality_acceptance"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Texture generation","interaction_type":"Pattern creation","satisfaction":3}],"purpose":"Exploring multiple interpretations and generating diverse options","effectiveness":0.7012330450644442,"reasoning":"Using AI to explore multiple interpretations and generate diverse solutions for ambiguous requirements"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":23.59606665605346,"cognitive_load":9.826642120960004,"satisfaction":5,"quality":3,"innovation":4,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":72.7,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"New project — Sunbrook Living, family building, spacious light-filled units, strong shared outdoor space. First concepts. \"Communal outdoor\" though — central courtyard the units wrap and overlook, or a rooftop the families ascend to? Courtyard gives eyes-on-kids, ground-level, everyday. Roof gives sun and view but it's a trip up. For families I lean courtyard as the heart. I'll sketch unit schemes with big windows, test a courtyard-wrapped scheme against a roof-terrace one, and check daylight orientation on each. Two directions to weigh.","enhanced_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution for Architecture","Address tight timeline for Architecture","Define project scope and constraints for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution","Address tight timeline","Define project scope and constraints"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Conflicting constraints in Architecture create genuine ambiguity about the right approach","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Managing multiple valid interpretations while maintaining design coherence","design_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions using analytical_pragmatic thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 47h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Technical specs"],"success_criteria":["Innovative solution delivered","Stakeholder approval achieved","Technical feasibility confirmed"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":1,"total_phases":8,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Residential Building Design","designer":"Designer_47","timestamp":"2024-05-17"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["Acceptable quality standards met","Innovative solutions developed","Delivered within timeline","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Approved","completion_date":"2024-07-08","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Sketched concept schemes prioritizing large windows and a central shared courtyard for families.","artifact":"Final deliverables","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering budget constraints"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":20,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Concept Development in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":2,"phase_name":"Schematic Design","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Lay out spacious multi-bedroom unit plans","Position communal outdoor terraces","Model massing for cross-ventilation"],"duration_estimate":37,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 5: Design Development.","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","utterance":"Concepts sketched — courtyard leaning ahead. Now plans and massing. But do the terraces belong stacked on each unit, private, or pooled into shared decks off the circulation? The brief says communal, yet families also want their own bit of outside. I'll do both at degrees — modest private balconies plus generous shared terraces on the courtyard side. Lay out the multi-bedroom units spacious, position the communal decks to catch afternoon sun, and shape the massing so air pulls through for cross-ventilation. Model it up.","continuity":" Transitioning from Vagueness in previous phase.","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["systematic_research","data_gathering","risk_analysis","problem_decomposition","bounded_rationality_acceptance"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Design iteration","interaction_type":"ControlNet guidance","satisfaction":5}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.7318057440885295,"reasoning":"Utilizing AI to gather missing information and explore potential scenarios under uncertainty"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":25.654879642140344,"cognitive_load":10.37808649563901,"satisfaction":5,"quality":2,"innovation":4,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":53.2,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Concepts sketched — courtyard leaning ahead. Now plans and massing. But do the terraces belong stacked on each unit, private, or pooled into shared decks off the circulation? The brief says communal, yet families also want their own bit of outside. I'll do both at degrees — modest private balconies plus generous shared terraces on the courtyard side. Lay out the multi-bedroom units spacious, position the communal decks to catch afternoon sun, and shape the massing so air pulls through for cross-ventilation. Model it up.","enhanced_requirements":["Finalize final assets for Architecture","Ensure quality standards are met for Architecture","Prepare handoff documentation for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Finalize final assets","Ensure quality standards are met","Prepare handoff documentation"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"External dependencies and unknowns block decision-making in Design Development","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Making progress despite missing critical information","design_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions using analytical_pragmatic thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 37h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: User research"],"success_criteria":["Innovative solution delivered","Stakeholder approval achieved","Technical feasibility confirmed"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":5,"total_phases":8,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Residential Building Design","designer":"Designer_47","timestamp":"2024-06-02"},"deliverables":["Floor plans","Elevations","Sections","Massing model"],"outcome_summary":["Quality improvements needed","Innovative solutions developed","Timeline challenges encountered","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"In Review","completion_date":"2024-03-07","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Produced floor plans and massing model arranging light-filled family units around communal terraces.","artifact":"Floor plans","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering tight timeline"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Floor plans","Elevations","Sections","Massing model"],"progress_percentage":100,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Schematic Design in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":4,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved"}},{"phase_number":3,"phase_name":"Design Development","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","requirements":["Detail balcony and courtyard connections","Refine window sizing for daylight","Resolve unit-to-communal-space transitions"],"duration_estimate":37,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 2: Zoning Review.","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","utterance":"Okay, schematic's done — units are ringed around the terraces, massing reads well. Now I resolve the sections. Balcony depth, that's the dial: 1.2 meters feels tight for a family, 2 metres starts eating the courtyard light below. Where's the line? Push it to 1.6, deep enough for a table, still lets sun into the court. Windows — how tall before it's a glass wall? Take sills to 400, heads near the slab. Draw the balcony-to-court connection detail, cut the wall section. Good, that transition holds.","continuity":" Transitioning from Ambiguity in previous phase.","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["set_specific_criteria","request_concrete_values","systematic_specification","bounded_rationality_acceptance"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":32.270715577942966,"cognitive_load":9.653358450901194,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":5,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":57.7,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase","Quality improvement from previous phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Okay, schematic's done — units are ringed around the terraces, massing reads well. Now I resolve the sections. Balcony depth, that's the dial: 1.2 meters feels tight for a family, 2 metres starts eating the courtyard light below. Where's the line? Push it to 1.6, deep enough for a table, still lets sun into the court. Windows — how tall before it's a glass wall? Take sills to 400, heads near the slab. Draw the balcony-to-court connection detail, cut the wall section. Good, that transition holds.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop design development based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider unclear requirements for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Develop design development based on previous phase","Consi