sketch the frontage rhythm. Log iterations. Concept schemes on the board.","continuity":"","style":"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["leverage_past_cases","pragmatic_approach","iterative_testing","constraint_as_creativity"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Design iteration","interaction_type":"ControlNet guidance","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Figma AI","purpose":"UI component generation","interaction_type":"Design system automation","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Exploring multiple interpretations and generating diverse options","effectiveness":0.854875858648118,"reasoning":"Using AI to explore multiple interpretations and generate diverse solutions for ambiguous requirements"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":47.73059713792392,"cognitive_load":9.658542794400356,"satisfaction":5,"quality":3,"innovation":4,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":41.6,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively","cognitive_style":"negotiative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Site's surveyed, sun and zoning are in. Now concept schemes. Human-scaled — how small is that? A 4 metre shopfront module reads intimate; 8 starts feeling corporate. It's a dial. And how tall before the street feels canyoned — four storeys, five? I'll keep the podium to three, set housing back above so the pedestrian sees a 12 metre street wall, not more. Test the retail-workspace-housing stack, sketch the frontage rhythm. Log iterations. Concept schemes on the board.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop concept development based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider tight timeline for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Develop concept development based on previous phase","Consider tight timeline","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Multiple v