fter considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Detailed plans","Building sections","Wall sections","3D model"],"progress_percentage":75,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Vagueness","Resolved through Applied to Design Development in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":5,"phase_name":"Material Specification","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Select cheapest compliant structural materials","Specify economical repeatable finishes","Confirm bulk material pricing"],"duration_estimate":46,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 1: Site Analysis.","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","utterance":"Plans and wall sections done. Now the actual materials. 'Cheapest compliant' — do I read that as lowest sticker price, or lowest installed cost including labor? Because ready-mix block is cheap to buy, slow to lay. Precast panels cost more upfront but crews fly. Two different budgets. Hmm. I'll price both bulk. Go blockwork structure, painted render finish, vinyl floors repeated every unit. Confirm the bulk pricing with the supplier, lock the spec. Repeatability is where the savings actually live.","continuity":"","style":"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["leverage_past_cases","pragmatic_approach","iterative_testing","constraint_as_creativity"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Figma AI","purpose":"Design consistency checking","interaction_type":"Rule-based analysis","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Style transfer","interaction_type":"Image-to-image","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Exploring multiple interpretations and generating diverse options","effectiveness":0.815104563520064,"reasoning":"Using AI to explore multiple interpretations and generate diverse solutions for ambiguous requirements"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":26.39