el_prototyping","constructive_thinking","abductive_reasoning_focus"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"ChatGPT","purpose":"Brainstorming design concepts","interaction_type":"Conversational prompting","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"Figma AI","purpose":"Design consistency checking","interaction_type":"Rule-based analysis","satisfaction":5}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.7706821197332101,"reasoning":"Utilizing AI to gather missing information and explore potential scenarios under uncertainty"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":50.45299826871629,"cognitive_load":10.79007433300849,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":3,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":42,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Starts with potential solutions to understand the problem","cognitive_style":"solution_focused","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Renders approved. Construction docs now. 'Dimensioned plan sets' — to what tolerance though. Full millimetre grid dims everywhere, or just the critical storefront and core lines. On a tight site every millimetre counts but over-dimensioning drowns the drawing. It's a matter of degree. I'll dimension tightly at the transfer and storefront junctions, looser on the repeating residential grid. Draft the plan set, detail the storefront-to-floor junction, prepare door and window schedules. Keep it readable.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop technical drawings based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider unclear requirements for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Develop technical drawings based on previous phase","Consider unclear requirements","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Critical information needed for Technical Coordination is not yet available","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Making progress despite missing critical information"