inst the servicing route. Let me pull the loading dock tighter to the transit edge so the deck columns land clean, then draw the unit-to-corridor wall section off that. There. Deck sits right now.","continuity":" Transitioning from Uncertainty in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["intuitive_exploration","creative_experimentation","trust_instinct","abductive_reasoning_focus"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"ChatGPT","purpose":"Brainstorming design concepts","interaction_type":"Conversational prompting","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"GitHub Copilot","purpose":"Code implementation","interaction_type":"Code completion","satisfaction":5}],"purpose":"Finding reference examples and validating intuitive decisions","effectiveness":0.9375028307100439,"reasoning":"Employing AI to externalize implicit knowledge and validate intuitive design decisions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":59.11604212613346,"cognitive_load":5.868642840472936,"satisfaction":5,"quality":5,"innovation":5,"efficiency":5},"actual_duration":26.8,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","Quality improvement from previous phase"],"framework_approach":"Starts with potential solutions to understand the problem","cognitive_style":"solution_focused","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Okay, schematic's approved, block's organized around the courtyard — now I actually resolve the amenity deck. Structural support for it... hm. The transfer down to the retail level below just feels wrong here, too heavy. Can't fully say why — it reads clumsy against the servicing route. Let me pull the loading dock tighter to the transit edge so the deck columns land clean, then draw the unit-to-corridor wall section off that. There. Deck sits right now.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop design development based on previous phase for Architecture","Consider unclear requirements for Architecture","Iterate based on feedback for Architecture"],"ori