mble the drawing set, compile the schedules, bundle for bidding. Permit-ready and priceable. Homes documented, out quick.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["systematic_research","data_gathering","risk_analysis","conversation_with_materials","reflection_in_action"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"GitHub Copilot","purpose":"Interaction logic","interaction_type":"Function suggestions","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"Midjourney","purpose":"Design inspiration","interaction_type":"Open exploration","satisfaction":5}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.882930413951533,"reasoning":"Utilizing AI to gather missing information and explore potential scenarios under uncertainty"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":68.16664961017678,"cognitive_load":11.091215830285163,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":3,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":40.7,"phase_insights":["High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection","cognitive_style":"reflective","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Details are drawn — now assemble the permit-ready set for Meadowgate Homes. \"Package for bidding\" — full spec book, or the trimmed schedule contractors actually want to price fast? Could read either way against the brief. Given it's fast-track I'll go lean: door and window schedules front, specs as a tight book, not an encyclopedia. Assemble the drawing set, compile the schedules, bundle for bidding. Permit-ready and priceable. Homes documented, out quick.","enhanced_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution for Architecture","Address budget constraints for Architecture","Define project scope and constraints for Architecture"],"original_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution","Address budget constraints","Define project scope and constraints"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"External dependencies and unknowns block decision-making in Site Analysis","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Making progress despite missing critical information","design_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection using reflective thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 46h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: User research"],"success_criteria":["High quality standards met","Design principles maintained","Stakeholder approval achieved"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":1,"total_phases":8,"domain":"Architecture","project_name":"Residential Building Design","designer":"Designer_53","timestamp":"2024-03-18"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Some creative elements incorporated","Delivered within timeline","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"In Review","completion_date":"2024-05-12","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Assembled the permit-ready construction document set with schedules and specifications for Meadowgate Homes.","artifact":"Design iterations","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering tight timeline"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":17,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Documentation in Architecture context"],"iteration_count":3,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved with minor revisions"}}],"project_outcomes":{"avg_quality":74.52262069524872,"final_quality":80.54710490244177,"quality_trend":"improving","avg_cognitive_load":8.949874121445415,"total_duration":281.4,"state_transitions":["Uncertainty → Vagueness","Vagueness → Ambiguity","Ambiguity → Vagueness","Vagueness → Tacit","Tacit → Vagueness","Vaguene