 I'll instrument both events this round and probe it in the sessions directly. Run the checkout tests, measure add-to-cart drop, A/B the filter placement. Friction points flagged, and I'll know the real culprit next read.","continuity":" Transitioning from Uncertainty in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["create_multiple_variations","visual_experimentation","broad_exploration","iterative_reflection_cycles","reflection_in_action"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"ChatGPT","purpose":"Generating design rationale","interaction_type":"Explanatory prompts","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Concretizing vague requirements and finding specific examples","effectiveness":0.8865359320370572,"reasoning":"Leveraging AI to clarify fuzzy requirements and generate concrete examples from vague descriptions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":28.167308591833184,"cognitive_load":8.769692430219155,"satisfaction":5,"quality":3,"innovation":5,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":46.4,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection","cognitive_style":"reflective","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Mockups approved — now usability testing on checkout, hunt the abandonment. Sessions I can run, drop-off I can measure. But I don't know yet whether the cart bleed is the surprise shipping cost or the forced account signup — the funnel data doesn't split those. So I'll instrument both events this round and probe it in the sessions directly. Run the checkout tests, measure add-to-cart drop, A/B the filter placement. Friction points flagged, and I'll know the real culprit next read.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop testing based on previous phase for Web Design","Consider budget constraints for Web Design","Iterate based on feedback for Web Design"],"original_requirements":["Develop testing based on previous 