:"Phase 6: Wireframing","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","utterance":"Sitemap's set, disciplines grouped. Now low-fi wireframes. \"Capability showcase\" — how deep does each one go? Could be a one-line badge, could be a full demo module with metrics. It's a spectrum and I keep sliding on it. I'll block it mid-weight: short claim, one proof visual, expand for detail. Project detail page: hero, problem, approach, outcome. Recruiter contact flow stays two fields, no friction. Sketching the boxes now. Wireframes drafted.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["request_clarification","bracket_interpretations","systematic_analysis","constraint_as_creativity","problem_reframing"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":33.01563869424426,"cognitive_load":7.705416767149511,"satisfaction":5,"quality":5,"innovation":4,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":40,"phase_insights":["Wireframing completed with vagueness resolved","Key challenge: tight timeline"],"framework_approach":"Applied to Wireframing in Web Design context","cognitive_style":"negotiative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Sitemap's set, disciplines grouped. Now low-fi wireframes. \"Capability showcase\" — how deep does each one go? Could be a one-line badge, could be a full demo module with metrics. It's a spectrum and I keep sliding on it. I'll block it mid-weight: short claim, one proof visual, expand for detail. Project detail page: hero, problem, approach, outcome. Recruiter contact flow stays two fields, no friction. Sketching the boxes now. Wireframes drafted.","enhanced_requirements":["Finalize prototypes for Web Design","Ensure quality standards are met for Web Design","Prepare handoff documentation for Web Design"],"original_requirements":["Finalize prototypes","Ensure quality standards are met","Prepare handoff documentation"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Vagueness in Wireframing due to unclear requirements","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Managing multiple valid interpretations while maintaining design coherence","design_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively using negotiative thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 22h allocated","Complexity: Medium","Dependencies: Technical specs"],"success_criteria":["High quality standards met","Stakeholder approval achieved","User testing validation"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":1,"total_phases":5,"domain":"Web Design","project_name":"Portfolio Website","designer":"Designer_58","timestamp":"2024-04-21"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Timeline challenges encountered","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Approved","completion_date":"2024-09-03","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Drafted low-fidelity wireframes for Volt & Ember project detail and capability showcase pages.","artifact":"Research documents","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on vagueness in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":100,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Vagueness","Resolved through Applied to Wireframing in Web Design context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved with minor revisions"}},{"phase_number":3,"phase_name":"Visual Design","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Tacit","requirements":["Define experimental tech visual language","Choose typography and accent palette","Style capability showcase mockups"],"duration_estimate":36,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 4: Interactive Elements.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Wireframes are blocked out, showcase depth decided. Now the visual language — experimental, technical. I keep pulling toward a dark mono base with one sharp accent, monospace for labels. Why? It just reads lab, not agency. Can't fully justify it beyond that — the softer rounded thing felt like a startup landing page, wrong room. Accent: an electric cyan, restrained. Grotesk for headers, mono for captions. Styling the capability mockups now. High-fi direction is set.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["externalize_knowledge","systematic_documentation","pattern_extraction","problem_reframing"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":36.11995022412455,"cognitive_load":7.187449761425277,"satisfaction":5,"quality":5,"innovation":4,"efficiency":4},"actual_duration":42.1,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively","cognitive_style":"negotiative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Wireframes are blocked out, showcase depth decided. Now the visual language — experimental, technical. I keep pulling toward a dark mono base with one sharp accent, monospace for labels. Why? It just reads lab, not agency. Can't fully justify it beyond that — the softer rounded thing felt like a startup landing page, wrong room. Accent: an electric cyan, restrained. Grotesk for headers, mono for captions. Styling the capability mockups now. High-fi direction is set.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop visual design based on previous phase for Web Design","Consider budget constraints for Web Design","Iterate based on feedback for Web Design"],"original_requirements":["Develop visual design based on previous phase","Consider budget constraints","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"The designer's implicit understanding guides decisions that are hard to articulate","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Articulating intuitive design decisions for stakeholder buy-in","design_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively using negotiative thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 36h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Stakeholder approval"],"success_criteria":["Technical feasibility confirmed","User testing validation","Design principles maintained"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":4,"total_phases":5,"domain":"Web Design","project_name":"Portfolio Website","designer":"Designer_58","timestamp":"2024-03-14"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Completed","completion_date":"2024-11-09","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Created a high-fidelity visual style expressing Volt & Ember' experimental, technical brand across key pages.","artifact":"Final deliverables","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on tacit in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":67,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Tacit","Resolved through Applied to Visual Design in Web Design context"],"iteration_count":2,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":4,"phase_name":"Interaction Design","complexity":"Medium","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","requirements":["Prototype interactive project demos","Design hover reveals for capabilities","Add scroll-triggered animations"],"duration_estimate":29,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 3: Layout Design.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Visual direction's locked — dark, mono accent, that lab feel. Now interaction. Interactive capability demos — but I don't know if these run on live data or canned clips. That changes everything: real demos need loading and error states, clips don't. I'll flag it for the eng check and build both a demo shell and a graceful fallback. Hover reveals on capabilities. Scroll-triggered animations, staggered as you enter each section. Prototyping the demos now. Interaction layer's in.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["externalize_knowledge","systematic_documentation","pattern_extraction","problem_reframing","constraint_as_creativity"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":35.53050823925159,"cognitive_load":4.754289405224072,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":4,"efficiency":5},"actual_duration":33.9,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively","cognitive_style":"negotiative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Visual direction's locked — dark, mono accent, that lab feel. Now interaction. Interactive capability demos — but I don't know if these run on live data or canned clips. That changes everything: real demos need loading and error states, clips don't. I'll flag it for the eng check and build both a demo shell and a graceful fallback. Hover reveals on capabilities. Scroll-triggered animations, staggered as you enter each section. Prototyping the demos now. Interaction layer's in.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop interaction design based on previous phase for Web Design","Consider tight timeline for Web Design","Iterate based on feedback for Web Design"],"original_requirements":["Develop interaction design based on previous phase","Consider tight timeline","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Pattern recognition from years of Web Design experience drives choices in Layout Design","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Articulating intuitive design decisions for stakeholder buy-in","design_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively using negotiative thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 29h allocated","Complexity: Medium","Dependencies: Technical specs"],"success_criteria":["User testing validation","Innovative solution delivered","Stakeholder approval achieved"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":3,"total_phases":5,"domain":"Web Design","project_name":"Portfolio Website","designer":"Designer_58","timestamp":"2024-10-17"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Completed","completion_date":"2024-07-12","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Prototyped interactive capability demos and scroll-triggered reveals for the Volt & Ember portfolio.","artifact":"Final deliverables","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on uncertainty in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering budget constraints"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":50,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Uncertainty","Resolved through Applied to Interaction Design in Web Design context"],"iteration_count":4,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":5,"phase_name":"Responsive Design","complexity":"Medium","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Adapt showcase grid for mobile","Set breakpoints for demo modules","Ensure touch-friendly interactions"],"duration_estimate":21,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 5: Development Handoff.","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","utterance":"Interactions are prototyped, demos have their fallback shell. Now mobile and tablet. \"Touch-friendly interactions\" — those scroll reveals were fine, but the hover capability reveals? On touch there's no hover. Do I make them tap-to-expand, or just show everything open? Two paths. I'll go tap-to-expand, keeps the scan clean. Showcase grid drops to single column on phone. Demo modules get their own breakpoint so they don't crush. Touch targets 44px min. Reflowed for mobile and tablet.","continuity":" Transitioning from Tacit in previous phase.","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["set_specific_criteria","request_concrete_values","systematic_specification","constraint_as_creativity","problem_solution_coevolution"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Figma AI","purpose":"Prototype interactions","interaction_type":"Smart animate","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"Claude","purpose":"Requirement analysis","interaction_type":"Structured analysis","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Concretizing vague requirements and finding specific examples","effectiveness":0.6646651490536118,"reasoning":"Leveraging AI to clarify fuzzy requirements and generate concrete examples from vague descriptions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":35.13423745525196,"cognitive_load":5.313590711317211,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":5,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":27.8,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively","cognitive_style":"negotiative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Interactions are prototyped, demos have their fallback shell. Now mobile and tablet. \"Touch-friendly interactions\" — those scroll reveals were fine, but the hover capability reveals? On touch there's no hover. Do I make them tap-to-expand, or just show everything open? Two paths. I'll go tap-to-expand, keeps the scan clean. Showcase grid drops to single column on phone. Demo modules get their own breakpoint so they don't crush. Touch targets 44px min. Reflowed for mobile and tablet.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop responsive design based on previous phase for Web Design","Consider budget constraints for Web Design","Iterate based on feedback for Web Design"],"original_requirements":["Develop responsive design based on previous phase","Consider budget constraints","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"The boundaries and success metrics for Development Handoff are fuzzy and subjective","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Transforming fuzzy requirements into concrete design decisions","design_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively using negotiative thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 21h allocated","Complexity: Medium","Dependencies: Technical specs"],"success_criteria":["Design principles maintained","High quality standards met","Innovative solution delivered"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":5,"total_phases":5,"domain":"Web Design","project_name":"Portfolio Website","designer":"Designer_58","timestamp":"2024-09-02"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Timeline challenges encountered","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"In Review","completion_date":"2024-12-22","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Adapted the Volt & Ember showcase grid and interactive demos for mobile and tablet screens.","artifact":"Research documents","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":83,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Responsive Design in Web Design context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved"}},{"phase_number":6,"phase_name":"Testing","complexity":"Medium","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Run usability tests with recruiters","Check demo performance across browsers","Fix navigation confusion points"],"duration_estimate":22,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 1: Content Strategy.","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","utterance":"Responsive is done, demos behave on touch. Last phase — testing with recruiters and partners. \"Fix navigation confusion\" — confusion could mean they can't find the work, or they find it but don't get what it is. Different fixes. Watching the sessions: recruiters overshoot capabilities looking for projects. So it's a labeling problem, not structure. I'll rename \"Capabilities\" clearer and surface work higher. Checked demos across Chrome, Safari, Firefox — one clip stutters, noted. Nav fixes shipped. Site's tested.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["request_clarification","bracket_interpretations","systematic_analysis","constraint_as_creativity","problem_reframing"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":33.01563869424426,"cognitive_load":7.705416767149511,"satisfaction":5,"quality":5,"innovation":4,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":40,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively","cognitive_style":"negotiative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Responsive is done, demos behave on touch. Last phase — testing with recruiters and partners. \"Fix navigation confusion\" — confusion could mean they can't find the work, or they find it but don't get what it is. Different fixes. Watching the sessions: recruiters overshoot capabilities looking for projects. So it's a labeling problem, not structure. I'll rename \"Capabilities\" clearer and surface work higher. Checked demos across Chrome, Safari, Firefox — one clip stutters, noted. Nav fixes shipped. Site's tested.","enhanced_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution for Web Design","Address unclear requirements for Web Design","Define project scope and constraints for Web Design"],"original_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution","Address unclear requirements","Define project scope and constraints"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"The requirements for Content Strategy can be satisfied in fundamentally different ways","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Managing multiple valid interpretations while maintaining design coherence","design_approach":"Redefines problems, uses constraints creatively using negotiative thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 22h allocated","Complexity: Medium","Dependencies: Technical specs"],"success_criteria":["High quality standards met","Stakeholder approval achieved","User testing validation"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":1,"total_phases":5,"domain":"Web Design","project_name":"Portfolio Website","designer":"Designer_58","timestamp":"2024-04-21"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Innovative solutions developed","Timeline challenges encountered","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Approved","completion_date":"2024-09-03","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Ran usability tests with recruiters and partners and fixed navigation issues on the Volt & Ember site.","artifact":"Review feedback","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback",