iction map underway.","continuity":" Transitioning from Ambiguity in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["create_multiple_variations","visual_experimentation","broad_exploration","frame_creation"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":77.96203212897238,"cognitive_load":6.735333994602249,"satisfaction":5,"quality":3,"innovation":4,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":25.9,"phase_insights":["Quality improvement from previous phase"],"framework_approach":"Creates entirely new frames for understanding problems","cognitive_style":"transformative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Saffron & Sage now — mobile shopping, streamline the purchase journey. Six phases this time. I survey mobile shopper behavior first. The friction... it's thumb reach, the buy button sitting too high, but I feel it more than I can chart it — you just sense the stretch is wrong. Comparing to apps that get it right, they anchor actions low. Noting conversion goals. Research doc and friction map underway.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop requirements gathering based on previous phase for Web Design","Consider tight timeline for Web Design","Iterate based on feedback for Web Design"],"original_requirements":["Develop requirements gathering based on previous phase","Consider tight timeline","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Qualitative requirements in Web Design leave significant room for interpretation","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Transforming fuzzy requirements into concrete design decisions","design_approach":"Creates entirely new frames for understanding problems using transformative thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 27h allocated","Complexity: Medium","Dependencies: User research"],"success_criteria":["Technical feasibility confirmed","User testing validation","Design principles maintained"]},"metadata":