ing multiple valid interpretations while maintaining design coherence","design_approach":"Creates entirely new frames for understanding problems using transformative thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 47h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Stakeholder approval"],"success_criteria":["Technical feasibility confirmed","Stakeholder approval achieved","Innovative solution delivered"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":3,"total_phases":8,"domain":"Web Design","project_name":"E-commerce Website Redesign","designer":"Designer_60","timestamp":"2024-05-06"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["Acceptable quality standards met","Innovative solutions developed","Delivered within timeline","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Completed","completion_date":"2024-08-19","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Designed mobile-first product and cart visuals for the Saffron & Sage storefront.","artifact":"Final deliverables","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on uncertainty in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering budget constraints"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":50,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Uncertainty","Resolved through Applied to Visual Design in Web Design context"],"iteration_count":2,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":3,"phase_name":"Interaction Design","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Prototype swipe and tap gestures","Design streamlined mobile checkout steps","Define loading and feedback states"],"duration_estimate":44,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 5: Visual Design.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Mobile visuals set — now they need to respond to touch. Swipe on product images: does swipe mean next photo, or next product? Both are conventions people expect. Guess wrong and it's jarring. I'll scope swipe to the gallery, next-product stays a tap — safer read. Prototyping the gestures, streamlined checkout steps, loading and feedback states so nothing feels frozen. Interactive prototype's ready for review.","continuity":" Transitioning from Vagueness in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["intuitive_exploration","creative_experimentation","trust_instinct","paradigm_shift_thinking"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"ChatGPT","purpose":"Brainstorming design concepts","interaction_type":"Conversational prompting","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"Figma AI","purpose":"UI component generation","interaction_type":"Design system automation","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Finding reference examples and validating intuitive decisions","effectiveness":0.7523529596414248,"reasoning":"Employing AI to externalize implicit knowledge and validate intuitive design decisions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":85.47494533022439,"cognitive_load":6.269302588518719,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":5,"efficiency":4},"actual_duration":26.9,"phase_insights":["High-quality output achieved","Quality improvement from previous phase"],"framework_approach":"Creates entirely new frames for understanding problems","cognitive_style":"transformative","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Mobile visuals set — now they need to respond to touch. Swipe on product images: does swipe mean next photo, or next product? Both are conventions people expect. Guess wrong and it's jarring. I'll scope swipe to the gallery, next-product stays a tap — safer read. Prototyping the gestures, streamlined checkout steps, loading and feedback states so nothing feels frozen. Interactive prototype's ready for review.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop interaction design based on previous phase for Web 