tial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":17,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Testing in Web Design context"],"iteration_count":2,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":6,"phase_name":"Development Handoff","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","requirements":["Export design tokens and specs","Annotate mobile breakpoints for devs","Package assets and prototype links"],"duration_estimate":43,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 6: Responsive Design.","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","utterance":"Testing's wrapped — last phase, hand it to the devs. 'Annotate breakpoints' — how much detail is enough? Every pixel spec, or the key rules and trust them? Over-annotate and they ignore it, under and they guess. I aim mid: tokens exported, the two breakpoints noted with reflow behavior, edge cases only where it's non-obvious. Assets packaged, prototype links attached. Handoff doc's done — that's the final deliverable.","continuity":" Transitioning from Tacit in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["prepare_multiple_scenarios","hypothesis_testing","parallel_prototyping","paradigm_shift_thinking","abductive_leap"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"GitHub Copilot","purpose":"Interaction logic","interaction_type":"Function suggestions","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"ChatGPT","purpose":"Generating design rationale","interaction_type":"Explanatory prompts","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.7970055716420985,"reasoning":"Utilizing AI to gather missing information and explore potential scenario