 in the doc so nobody merges them. Exporting screen specs and assets, documenting the animation and security states, briefing engineers on the transfer edge cases, edge states named explicitly.","continuity":"","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["prepare_multiple_scenarios","hypothesis_testing","parallel_prototyping","bounded_rationality_acceptance","satisficing_approach"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"GitHub Copilot","purpose":"Code implementation","interaction_type":"Code completion","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Figma AI","purpose":"Layout suggestions","interaction_type":"Auto-layout","satisfaction":3}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.9497434282679926,"reasoning":"Utilizing AI to gather missing information and explore potential scenarios under uncertainty"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":23.576224023838304,"cognitive_load":10.799708520885872,"satisfaction":5,"quality":2,"innovation":4,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":69,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified","High cognitive load - challenging phase"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Testing wrapped, iterations folded in — now hand it to engineering. This transfer edge-case note, though: 'insufficient funds' state. Does that mean the hard-decline screen, or the soft warning before they confirm? Both live in the flow and I speced them separately. I'll spell out which is which in the doc so nobody merges them. Exporting screen specs and assets, documenting the animation and security states, briefing engineers on the transfer edge cases, edge states named explicitly.","enhanced_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution for UI/UX Design","Address budget constraints for UI/UX Design","Define project scope and constraints for UI/UX Design"],"original_requireme