","deliverables_produced":["User interview transcripts","Persona cards","Journey maps","Research insights deck"],"progress_percentage":83,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to User Research in UI/UX Design context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved"}},{"phase_number":2,"phase_name":"Information Architecture","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Tacit","requirements":["Card-sort data view categories","Define dashboard navigation hierarchy","Simplify metric grouping structure"],"duration_estimate":50,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 4: Data Visualization.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Personas are set, filter-drowning is the through-line — now the architecture. Card sort's on the wall. This grouping just feels right — campaign metrics up top, account health beneath. Why? Can't fully justify it, it reads clean, matches how they talked. This other version, everything alphabetized, technically valid but it's dead, no rhythm. Trusting the first one. Navigation two levels deep max, metrics grouped by workflow not data type. Locking the hierarchy.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["externalize_knowledge","systematic_documentation","pattern_extraction","conversation_with_materials","iterative_reflection_cycles"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":56.92047561806977,"cognitive_load":7.10078104531079,"satisfaction":5,"quality":5,"innovation":3,"efficiency":5},"actual_duration":45,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Continuous dialogue between action and reflection","cognitive_style":"reflective","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Personas are set, filter-drowning is the through-line — now the architecture. Card sort's on the wall. This grouping just feels right — campaign metrics up top, account health beneath. 