vative solutions developed","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Completed","completion_date":"2024-12-25","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Produced high-fidelity mockups and a component library for Tessellate's analytics dashboard, standardizing chart styles and KPI tiles.","artifact":"High-fidelity mockups","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["High-fidelity mockups","Design system","Component library","Style guide"],"progress_percentage":83,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Visual Design in UI/UX Design context"],"iteration_count":4,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved"}},{"phase_number":5,"phase_name":"Usability Testing","complexity":"Medium","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","requirements":["Recruit dashboard power-users for testing","Run task-based sessions on data filtering","Log clarity issues and iterate mockups"],"duration_estimate":27,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 6: Developer Handoff.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Right, mockups and the component library are built — time to put the filter controls in front of real people. And 'confusion' is a matter of degree. One power-user pausing two seconds isn't a problem; three of five backtracking on the date filter is. Where's my line? I'll call it: task fails or two-plus mis-clicks, that's a fix. Run the task-based sessions, log the analytics-layout stumbles, tally against that bar. Filter dropdown's clearly over the line. Iterating the mockup now.","continuity":"","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["intuitive_exploration","creative_experimentation","trust_instinct","abductive_leap","paradigm_shift_thinking"],"ai_usage