onas drafted — now structure the IA. Grouping metrics by client and campaign. This grouping just feels right — top level by client, campaigns nested, alerts floating above. Can't lay out a clean rule for why alerts break the hierarchy, they just need to. Like triage — the urgent thing shouldn't be three clicks down. Running a card sort to check my gut against real users, defining the role-based nav. At-a-glance means shallow. Nineteen years says trust the sort, not just the feel.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop information architecture based on previous phase for UI/UX Design","Consider budget constraints for UI/UX Design","Iterate based on feedback for UI/UX Design"],"original_requirements":["Develop information architecture based on previous phase","Consider budget constraints","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Success in Data Visualization relies heavily on experiential knowledge and intuition","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Articulating intuitive design decisions for stakeholder buy-in","design_approach":"Starts with potential solutions to understand the problem using solution_focused thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 35h allocated","Complexity: High","Dependencies: Stakeholder approval"],"success_criteria":["High quality standards met","Stakeholder approval achieved","User testing validation"]},"metadata":{"phase_index":4,"total_phases":6,"domain":"UI/UX Design","project_name":"SaaS Dashboard Redesign","designer":"Designer_70","timestamp":"2024-03-10"},"deliverables":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"outcome_summary":["High quality output achieved","Some creative elements incorporated","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Approved","completion_date":"2024-02-06","sign_off":"Client approved"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Structured a role-based information architecture grouping client campaign metrics into an 