able campaign-metrics overview with per-client drilldown and role-switching flows.","artifact":"Low-fidelity wireframes","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on vagueness in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering tight timeline"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Low-fidelity wireframes","User flows","Information architecture","Clickable prototype"],"progress_percentage":86,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Vagueness","Resolved through Applied to Wireframing in UI/UX Design context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":4,"phase_name":"Visual Design","complexity":"Medium","cognitive_state":"Uncertainty","requirements":["design decluttered metric cards","establish status color coding","build charting component set"],"duration_estimate":24,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 3: Component Design.","cognitive_state":"Tacit","utterance":"Wireframes are set — now hi-fi and the status colors. Designing metric cards. What I don't have yet is the actual threshold values from the client — what counts as red versus amber on spend pacing? Without those the color coding is a guess. I'll build the system with placeholder breakpoints and mark them for the data team to fill. Designing decluttered cards, three-tier status palette, colorblind-safe. Building the charting set. Nineteen years — I spec the color logic so plugging real numbers is trivial later.","continuity":" Transitioning from Vagueness in previous phase.","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["intuitive_exploration","creative_experimentation","trust_instinct","abductive_reasoning_focus","solution_led_exploration"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Claude","purpose":"Design critique and feedback","interaction_type":"Analytical dialogue","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Midjourney","purpose":"Material and texture studies","interact