 motion. Prepping test scenarios around finding a flagged campaign. Interactive prototype's running.","continuity":"","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["intuitive_exploration","creative_experimentation","trust_instinct","constructive_thinking","abductive_reasoning_focus"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Claude","purpose":"Requirement analysis","interaction_type":"Structured analysis","satisfaction":4},{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Rapid prototyping visuals","interaction_type":"Local generation","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Finding reference examples and validating intuitive decisions","effectiveness":0.8672489335770318,"reasoning":"Employing AI to externalize implicit knowledge and validate intuitive design decisions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":89.32233937963844,"cognitive_load":5.9555198323212,"satisfaction":5,"quality":4,"innovation":3,"efficiency":4},"actual_duration":23.9,"phase_insights":["High-quality output achieved","Quality improvement from previous phase"],"framework_approach":"Starts with potential solutions to understand the problem","cognitive_style":"solution_focused","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Cards and color system locked — now prototype the interactions. Animating the threshold alerts. Though \"alert\" reads two ways — a passive color shift on the card, or an active thing that pushes to the top and pulses? Managers-at-a-glance argues for the push. But that could feel noisy. I'll prototype the pulse-and-promote, keep passive as the test comparison. Wiring live campaign views, specced the alert motion. Prepping test scenarios around finding a flagged campaign. Interactive prototype's running.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop prototyping based on previous phase for UI/UX Design","Consider unclear requirements for UI/UX Design","Iterate based on feedback for UI/UX Design"],"original_requirements":["Develop prototyping based on previous phase","Consider unclear r