","Completed ahead of schedule","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"Completed","completion_date":"2024-05-14","sign_off":"Internal review complete"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Built an interactive prototype demonstrating dataset filtering, sorting, and view-switching interactions.","artifact":"Micro-interactions","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on ambiguity in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering budget constraints"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Interactive prototype","Micro-interactions","Animation specs","Usability test plan"],"progress_percentage":17,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Ambiguity","Resolved through Applied to Prototyping in UI/UX Design context"],"iteration_count":2,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":5,"phase_name":"Usability Testing","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Ambiguity","requirements":["Test navigation with operations analysts","Measure dataset task completion times","Capture feedback for design iterations"],"duration_estimate":50,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 5: Interaction Design.","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","utterance":"Prototype's live, filtering and sorting demo well. Now testing with the ops analysts. This feedback though — 'the drill-down is slow.' Slow to load, or slow to find? Those are opposite fixes. One's engineering, one's my IA. Watching the recordings: they hesitate at the second-level nav, so it's findability. Good, that's mine. Logging completion times, task three's at 40 seconds, too long. Capturing the pattern, writing the iteration notes. Moving forward.","continuity":" Transitioning from Uncertainty in previous phase.","style":"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["gradual_refinement","incremental_adjustments","feedback_driven","abductive_reasoning_focus","constructive_thinking"],"ai_usage":{"use