ally and start stacking? I'll call it: 1024 holds full grid, below that pin two columns and scroll. Annotating every data-grid state — empty, loading, error, overflow. Packaging specs and assets. Handoff shipped.","continuity":"","style":"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["gradual_refinement","incremental_adjustments","feedback_driven","abductive_reasoning_focus","constructive_thinking"],"ai_usage":{"used":false,"tools":[],"reasoning":"Manual design process for this phase"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":31.856564177803968,"cognitive_load":6.219973088920386,"satisfaction":5,"quality":3,"innovation":4,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":31.2,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Starts with potential solutions to understand the problem","cognitive_style":"solution_focused","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Testing's done, iterations locked from the analyst runs. Now the engineering handoff. 'Responsive' — where's the breakpoint though? A data grid doesn't collapse like marketing pages. At what width does the table stop scrolling horizontally and start stacking? I'll call it: 1024 holds full grid, below that pin two columns and scroll. Annotating every data-grid state — empty, loading, error, overflow. Packaging specs and assets. Handoff shipped.","enhanced_requirements":["Finalize final assets for UI/UX Design","Ensure quality standards are met for UI/UX Design","Prepare handoff documentation for UI/UX Design"],"original_requirements":["Finalize final assets","Ensure quality standards are met","Prepare handoff documentation"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"Qualitative requirements in UI/UX Design leave significant room for interpretation","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Transforming fuzzy requirements into concrete design decisions","design_approach":"Starts with potential solutions to understand the problem using solution_focused thinking","key_constraints":["Timeline: 20h allocate