allenges encountered","Stakeholders highly satisfied"],"completion_status":{"status":"In Review","completion_date":"2024-11-10","sign_off":"Ready for next phase"},"cognitive_decision_step":{"action":"Developed a primary and accent color palette for Marlowe & Vane and validated contrast across digital and print applications.","artifact":"Review feedback","rationale":{"initial":"Initial approach based on uncertainty in requirements","improved":"Refined approach after considering unclear requirements"}},"phase_outcome":{"completion_status":"Completed","deliverables_produced":["Research documents","Design iterations","Review feedback","Final deliverables"],"progress_percentage":43,"key_decisions":["Decision based on Uncertainty","Resolved through Applied to Color Development in Graphic Design context"],"iteration_count":5,"stakeholder_approval":"Approved after iterations"}},{"phase_number":5,"phase_name":"Layout Design","complexity":"High","cognitive_state":"Tacit","requirements":["Apply logo to stationery mockups","Layout business cards and letterhead","Test grid across touchpoints"],"duration_estimate":46,"think_aloud":{"phase_context":"Phase 4: Logo Design.","cognitive_state":"Vagueness","utterance":"Palette's in, ratios defined. Now applying across stationery. This business card... the aperture mark sits fine, but centered it feels timid — and 'confident-refined' was the whole read. I can't point to a metric, it just wants tension. Nudge the mark to the lower-left corner, let the accent bleed off one edge. Yes — that's it, reads assured now. Same logic to the letterhead, testing the grid across both. Stationery composed.","continuity":"","style":"converger","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["set_specific_criteria","request_concrete_values","systematic_specification","frame_creation","paradigm_shift_thinking"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Midjourney","purpose":"Material and texture studies","interaction_type"