:"refiner","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["gradual_refinement","incremental_adjustments","feedback_driven","constructive_thinking","solution_led_exploration"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Stable Diffusion","purpose":"Design iteration","interaction_type":"ControlNet guidance","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Midjourney","purpose":"Concept visualization","interaction_type":"Creative generation","satisfaction":4}],"purpose":"Concretizing vague requirements and finding specific examples","effectiveness":0.8192250356136497,"reasoning":"Leveraging AI to clarify fuzzy requirements and generate concrete examples from vague descriptions"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":62.714045590164055,"cognitive_load":5.869554674090801,"satisfaction":5,"quality":3,"innovation":5,"efficiency":3},"actual_duration":30.6,"phase_insights":["3D Rendering completed with tacit resolved","Key challenge: unclear requirements"],"framework_approach":"Starts with potential solutions to understand the problem","cognitive_style":"solution_focused","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Seating's specced — renders now for the client. I drop the finish palette into the dining room view and the flooring color just... fights the banquette fabric. Can't name the rule, it's a feel thing after twenty years. Warm the floor tone a notch, and there — it settles. Test two colorways in the render to be sure. Client-ready views of the dining room, morning and evening light. Renders produced, view studies out.","enhanced_requirements":["Develop 3d rendering based on previous phase for Interior Design","Consider tight timeline for Interior Design","Iterate based on feedback for Interior Design"],"original_requirements":["Develop 3d rendering based on previous phase","Consider tight timeline","Iterate based on feedback"],"cognitive_state_rationale":"The boundaries and success metrics for Material Selection are fuzzy and subjective","design_context":{"current_challenge":"Tra