quence internal first, then external same-week. Coordinate the phased announcement, deliver the updated asset package, announce the reposition to market. Refresh is launched. That's the project.","continuity":"","style":"explorer","generation_method":"framework_based","framework_influenced":true},"behaviors":["prepare_multiple_scenarios","hypothesis_testing","parallel_prototyping","satisficing_approach"],"ai_usage":{"used":true,"tools":[{"tool":"Midjourney","purpose":"Aesthetic exploration","interaction_type":"Style prompting","satisfaction":5},{"tool":"Claude","purpose":"Design critique and feedback","interaction_type":"Analytical dialogue","satisfaction":5}],"purpose":"Researching data, analyzing trends, and gathering information","effectiveness":0.7035604409025693,"reasoning":"Utilizing AI to gather missing information and explore potential scenarios under uncertainty"},"outcomes":{"design_quality":47.063757173037274,"cognitive_load":6.705057036747132,"satisfaction":5,"quality":2,"innovation":3,"efficiency":2},"actual_duration":37.6,"phase_insights":["Quality concerns identified"],"framework_approach":"Breaks problems down, seeks good-enough solutions","cognitive_style":"analytical_pragmatic","ultra_realistic_think_aloud":"Applications applied and approved — final phase, launch. 'Phased rollout' — phased over what, days or weeks? And does the market announcement lead the visual switch or follow it? For a reposition I'd usually reveal the new look and message together so the story's coherent. I'll sequence internal first, then external same-week. Coordinate the phased announcement, deliver the updated asset package, announce the reposition to market. Refresh is launched. That's the project.","enhanced_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution for Brand Design","Address budget constraints for Brand Design","Define project scope and constraints for Brand Design"],"original_requirements":["Understand innovative design solution","Address budget constraints